From 6e8deca978fe17fe938bdd7897a51a0618edb894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:11:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup)!: one WCS per setup; G54-G59 is only the setup's
 post label

A setup now owns exactly one work coordinate system: SetupDef.wcs names
one entity (was a six-slot list) and SetupDef.work_offset is only the
word the post writes for it - relabelling moves no origin and no height.
The browser shows one row, plain "WCS" (its word as the faint suffix),
never G54..G59 slot rows; it targets the WCS page, which edits the
active setup's origin through the undoable SetWcs. SetWcsOrigin::new
takes no slot; UiTarget::WcsSlot(i) became UiTarget::Wcs. The setup
sheet, WCS page, rotation refusal, MCP get_job and height chips speak
of "WCS (G55)" / "WCS G55".

Project v54 (project::wcs_one): each v53 setup keeps the entity (name
and placement) of the slot it posted, so single-WCS documents post byte
for byte; placed slots no setup posted are dropped with a load note
(project::open_noted / load_noted, shown in the status line); a
no-setup document keeps G54; an operation in a setup the file lacks
keeps its zero (<setup>/G54 -> <setup>/WCS). Two origins inside one
setup only arise from v51-or-older files, which the v52 rung already
refuses by name. The two-setups-same-word refusal stands.

BREAKING CHANGE: project files are v54 ("wcs" is one name, unreadable
by older builds); placed work-offset slots no setup posted are dropped
on load (with a note); SetWcsOrigin::new lost its slot argument.

Fixes #342

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
